      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the OOMKill is persistent despite seemingly adequate limits, the suspicion shifts toward a leak or an aggressive probe. First, try temporarily disabling the liveness probe completely and monitor the pod's logs over an extended period to see if it self-terminates without the probe intervention. If it runs stable without the probe, the probe might be faulty or too sensitive. If it still crashes, increase the memory limits significantly as a test to rule out an underestimated baseline requirement.",
